// With the default strategy, a rule that cannot win is not evaluated: a rule
// whose `concept is "leave"` clause cannot hold, and a rule less specific than
// an eligible one. Evaluating `nothing_here and ...` would be an error (the
// name is undefined), so the lines below play only because those rules are
// left alone. This is the documented consequence of that shortcut.

state
  concept: "greet"
  gold: 20

beat Start
  Bark()
  Bark()

beat Bark
  when
    nothing_here and concept is "leave"
      Not evaluated: the concept clause cannot hold.
    gold > 10 and concept is "greet"
      Rich greeting.
    nothing_here
      Not evaluated: less specific than the eligible rule above.
    true
      Nothing.

/*
<test>
- expected: |
    ~ Rich greeting.

    ~ Rich greeting.
</test>
*/
